                <pb facs="0041" n="31" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg31"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/1089: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-28T11:00:00-04:00">October 28, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>206. From Braden for the Under Secretary of State. Add the following to my 205,
                    October 28, 9 a.m. In my opinion a final intensive drive to settle the
                    fundamental question should be made and to this end the situation should be
                    presented to the other mediatory Foreign Offices, their opinions requested and a
                    concrete program of the complete unity of action laid down for the Conference.
                    By reason of its location to and detachment from conflicting problems the
                    Department of State logically should make this <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >démarche</hi>. As soon as we have determined just what security <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> may be obtained in the Chaco I shall
                    transmit my specific recommendations in this particular. [Braden.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
